<p>Former Bulgarian president Rumen Radev and his new Progressive Bulgaria coalition appeared set to win Bulgaria’s parliamentary election on April 19, with exit polls and early counts putting the alliance at around 39% to 45% of the vote. That left it well ahead of the liberal PP-DB coalition and the GERB party of former prime minister Boyko Borissov. Several outlets said the result could give Radev’s bloc an outright majority in the 240-seat National Assembly, potentially ending a long stretch of unstable coalition politics after Bulgaria’s eighth election in five years. Radev, who left the presidency in January to lead the new coalition, campaigned on fighting corruption and dismantling what he called Bulgaria’s “oligarchic governance model.” That message landed after years of political deadlock and public frustration with the judiciary and entrenched elites. At the same time, his softer stance toward Moscow, criticism of some EU policies, and opposition to military aid for Ukraine have drawn close attention across Europe. Even so, he has also described his goal as a “democratic, modern, European Bulgaria” and suggested he could work with pro-EU reformists on judicial change.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/fb4IbUfxEukBgyKBv8kHBf6M9l8Fu6STqScsRA61T6eztQilKAraTLS8TmOQzEwA3IgdFjWDwkvPTLKKp-7_pPWyyu_yMTXqLKUx2A-ZmacaKRerUGxENfIqKQcZPGG4pAbcSHSLK7hlElZQopVcy0QfbQNvKeixnWOZ1liwqlbM297UrolPgYPBUNGtMmXVYhcqmZMrjNZINcAnJStydh_OqMwpxPJmG77JsQR4jGzH36MoPGBausEDOfDUr3uj095KkKAqVGYyONJTLw' alt='&quot;Progressive Bulgaria&quot; coalition&#x27;s leader and former President Rumen Radev speaks to the press at his party headquarters after polls closed in Bulgaria&#x27;s parliamentary elections in Sofia on April 19, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Old parties slump: Preliminary results showed GERB at about 13% and DPS-New Beginning at about 6%, a sharp setback for parties critics tied to Bulgaria’s old patronage networks.</li><li>Victory rhetoric: As projections rolled in, Radev called the result a “victory of hope,” framing the landslide as a broader political reset rather than just a party win.</li><li>Borissov response: Former prime minister Boyko Borissov congratulated Radev while warning that “winning elections is one thing, governing is another,” underscoring the challenge of turning a strong mandate into durable rule.</li><li>Voter priorities: Some voters said they wanted sweeping change centered on the judicial system and corruption, including Sofia retiree Stiliana Andonova, who said “everything simply has to change”.</li></ul><blockquote>We voted in numbers, we defeated apathy. But distrust in Bulgarian politics is still high and we have a lot of work ahead of us. This is just the first step. - Rumen Radev</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Rumen Radev: He cast GERB and DPS-New Beginning as enablers of a “mafia state,” presenting his win as a mandate to break up Bulgaria’s old patronage order. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/bulgaria-election-russia-rumen-radev-win-exit-poll/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>PP-DB coalition: Though far behind Radev, the liberal reformist bloc also treated the outcome as a blow to the old power structure, letting it argue that the vote validated its long-running anti-oligarchic case rather than simply handing it a defeat. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/bulgaria-election-russia-rumen-radev-win-exit-poll/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Bulgarian voters: For some voters, demands for cleaner courts and less corruption were tied to hopes for a more prosperous, more normal European life, not just a change in parties. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/19/world/europe/bulgaria-elections-results.html'>The New York Times</a>, <a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993379/bulgarias-pro-russian-ex-president-leads-in-snap-vote-exit-polls'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cm2kgm1zpgro'>Rumen Radev set to win Bulgarian Parliamentary election</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/bulgaria-election-russia-rumen-radev-win-exit-poll/'>Russia-aligned Rumen Radev wins landslide in Bulgaria</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/former-president-rumen-radev-will-win-bulgaria-election-exit-poll-suggests'>Former president Rumen Radev will win Bulgaria election, exit poll suggests</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/19/world/europe/bulgaria-elections-results.html'>Bulgarian Voters Back New Political Coalition Led by Radev</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/19/bulgaria-election-rumen-radev-boyko-borissov'>Bulgaria’s former president claims ‘victory’ after projections show him winning parliamentary elections</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-pro-russian-radev-leading-after-parliamentary-vote-exit-polls-show/a-76846189'>Bulgaria: Pro-Russian Radev leading after parliamentary vote, exit polls show</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/exit-poll-suggests-center-left-coalition-former-president-132187377'>Exit poll suggests the center-left coalition of former president Rumen Radev will win Bulgaria election</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/19/exit-poll-shows-former-president-radevs-party-set-to-win-bulgaria-election'>Bulgaria election: Ex-President Radev claims ‘victory’ after early results</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/bulgaria%27s-pro-russian-former-president-set-for-strong-election-win-exit-polls-show'>Bulgaria&#x27;s pro-Russian former president set for strong election win, exit polls show</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1993379/bulgarias-pro-russian-ex-president-leads-in-snap-vote-exit-polls'>Bulgaria’s pro-Russian ex-president leads in snap vote: exit polls</a> - dawn.com</li><